WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:07.791
Throughout July, Pollyanna often told Aunt Polly how happy she was.

2
00:00:07.792 --> 00:00:14.054
Aunt Polly usually replied, "It's nice that your days are happy, but that's not enough.

3
00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:20.242
They must also be profitable, or I've failed in my duty to you."

4
00:00:20.243 --> 00:00:26.521
Pollyanna answered with hugs and kisses, which Aunt Polly found alarming.

5
00:00:26.522 --> 00:00:31.224
But one day during a sewing lesson, Pollyanna asked.

6
00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:35.679
"What does having a 'profitable' day mean?"

7
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:41.305
"Why, it means having something to show for the day," Aunt Polly said.

8
00:00:41.306 --> 00:00:45.867
"So, just being glad isn't profitable?"

9
00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:51.451
"Certainly not." Aunt Polly rapped her thimble on the table.

10
00:00:51.452 --> 00:00:56.844
"Oh! Then I'm afraid you'll never want to play the game."

11
00:00:56.845 --> 00:01:00.336
"Game? What game?"

12
00:01:00.337 --> 00:01:08.386
"The game that Fath—" Pollyanna clapped her hand over her mouth. "I mean, it's nothing."

13
00:01:08.387 --> 00:01:14.730
"That's enough for this morning," Aunt Polly said, and their sewing lesson was over.

14
00:01:14.731 --> 00:01:20.817
*** That afternoon Pollyanna was going down the attic stairs when she met Aunt Polly coming

15
00:01:20.818 --> 00:01:25.196
up. "You're coming to see me!" Pollyanna cried with

16
00:01:25.197 --> 00:01:29.717
delight. She scampered back up the stairs and threw open her door in

17
00:01:29.718 --> 00:01:33.045
welcome. Aunt Polly had not intended to visit her niece.

18
00:01:33.046 --> 00:01:37.963
Instead she'd planned to look for a shawl in the main part of the attic.

19
00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:42.592
So she was surprised to find herself sitting in a chair in Pollyanna's room.

20
00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:47.932
Then again, she'd often found herself doing surprising things since Pollyanna's arrival.

21
00:01:47.933 --> 00:01:52.080
"I love having visitors!" Pollyanna said.

22
00:01:52.081 --> 00:02:00.211
"And I love this room, even though it doesn't have the carpets and curtains and pictures I—" She stopped short.

23
00:02:00.212 --> 00:02:05.404
Her aunt looked at her. "What's that, Pollyanna?"

24
00:02:05.405 --> 00:02:13.202
Pollyanna turned red with embarrassment. "I didn't mean to say that."

25
00:02:13.203 --> 00:02:18.630
"Maybe not." There was a note of coldness in Aunt Polly's voice.

26
00:02:18.631 --> 00:02:23.028
"But you did say it, so let's hear the rest."

27
00:02:23.029 --> 00:02:29.795
"It was nothing really, just that I'd been planning on pretty carpets and lace curtains and—"

28
00:02:29.796 --> 00:02:34.396
"Planning on them?" Aunt Polly interrupted sharply.

29
00:02:34.397 --> 00:02:38.640
Pollyanna turned even redder as she tried to apologize.

30
00:02:38.641 --> 00:02:42.752
"It was only because I'd never had pretty things.

31
00:02:42.753 --> 00:02:46.786
I mean, we had two rugs from the donation box.

32
00:02:46.787 --> 00:02:51.329
But one had ink spots and the other had holes.

33
00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:55.842
And Fath—I mean, we had two nice pictures.

34
00:02:55.843 --> 00:03:02.350
We sold one though to buy me shoes, and the glass broke on another one."

35
00:03:02.351 --> 00:03:06.599
Aunt Polly listened without interrupting as Pollyanna went on.

36
00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:13.540
"When I walked through your house that first day, I shouldn't have been planning how pretty my room would be.

37
00:03:13.541 --> 00:03:19.615
But truly, Aunt Polly, in only a few minutes I was glad that this was my room.

38
00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:26.657
I was so glad that the bureau didn't have a mirror because I didn't want to see my freckles!

39
00:03:26.658 --> 00:03:31.464
There couldn't be a nicer picture than the view from my window.

40
00:03:31.465 --> 00:03:34.809
And you've been so good to me."

41
00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.928
Now it was Aunt Polly's turn to blush.

42
00:03:37.929 --> 00:03:44.924
She suddenly rose to her feet and said stiffly, "You've said quite enough."

43
00:03:44.925 --> 00:03:50.675
The next minute Aunt Polly swept downstairs, leaving a baffled Pollyanna behind.

44
00:03:50.676 --> 00:03:58.117
It was only when Aunt Polly reached the first floor that she realized she'd forgotten the shawl.

45
00:03:58.118 --> 00:04:00.526
*** In the morning Aunt Polly spoke to

46
00:04:00.527 --> 00:04:06.413
Nancy. "Today you may move Miss Pollyanna's things to the room

47
00:04:06.414 --> 00:04:10.831
below." "Yes, ma'am," Nancy said quietly.

48
00:04:10.832 --> 00:04:17.160
A few minutes later, Nancy broke the happy news to Pollyanna in the attic.

49
00:04:17.161 --> 00:04:20.042
Nancy gathered up an armload of clothes.

50
00:04:20.043 --> 00:04:24.799
"I'll hurry and take your things down before Miss Polly changes her mind."

51
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:30.331
Pollyanna went flying downstairs, taking the steps two at a time.

52
00:04:30.332 --> 00:04:35.387
She banged two doors and knocked over a chair before finding her aunt in the sitting room.

53
00:04:35.388 --> 00:04:43.781
"Oh, Aunt Polly, thank you! That room has everything I ever wanted!"

54
00:04:43.782 --> 00:04:50.517
"I'm glad you like it, and I trust you'll take proper care of everything," Aunt Polly said.

55
00:04:50.518 --> 00:04:55.323
"But please pick up that chair, and stop banging doors."

56
00:04:55.324 --> 00:05:00.922
She would have said more, but for some strange reason, she felt like crying.

57
00:05:00.923 --> 00:05:05.632
"I'm sorry I banged the doors, but I was just so happy!

58
00:05:05.633 --> 00:05:09.343
Did you ever bang doors when you were happy?"

59
00:05:09.344 --> 00:05:14.357
"Certainly not!" Aunt Polly was shocked at the thought.

60
00:05:14.358 --> 00:05:19.780
"Oh, that's a shame because that means you were never glad about something."

61
00:05:19.781 --> 00:05:25.968
Before Aunt Polly could reply, Pollyanna dashed back upstairs to help Nancy move her things.

